1
00:01:44,000 --> 00:01:50,000
The Small One is a animation, family film directed by Don Bluth.

2
00:03:28,000 --> 00:03:34,000
Ordered by his father to sell an old mule called Small One, a Hebrew boy in
the ancient Holy Land takes the donkey to the Jerusalem market.

3
00:05:12,000 --> 00:05:18,000
Finding no buyers there, the boy is about to give up when he meets a kind man named Joseph, who
buys Small One and uses the steed to take his pregnant wife Mary to Bethlehem.

4
00:06:56,000 --> 00:07:02,000
Boy (voice), played by Sean Marshall.

5
00:08:40,000 --> 00:08:46,000
Tanner (voice), played by William Woodson.

6
00:10:24,000 --> 00:10:30,000
Father (voice), played by Olan Soule.

7
00:12:08,000 --> 00:12:14,000
Guard (voice), played by Joe Higgins.

8
00:13:52,000 --> 00:13:58,000
Joseph (voice), played by Gordon Jump.

9
00:15:36,000 --> 00:15:42,000
Auctioneer (voice), played by Hal Smith.

10
00:17:20,000 --> 00:17:26,000
The Small One (also known as A Christmas Miracle in the UK) is a 1978 American animated featurette produced by Walt Disney
Productions and released theatrically by Buena Vista Distribution on December 16, 1978, with a re-issue of Pinocchio (1940).

11
00:19:04,000 --> 00:19:10,000
The story is based on a 1947 children's book of the same name by Charles Tazewell and was a project for the new
generation of Disney animators including Don Bluth, Jerry Rees, Henry Selick, Gary Goldman, and John Pomeroy.

12
00:20:48,000 --> 00:20:54,000
The story tells of a young boy outside Nazareth, who must part
with his best friend, an old donkey named Small One.

13
00:22:32,000 --> 00:22:38,000
He brings it to market, but no one is in need of a
"scrawny donkey", except for a tanner.

14
00:24:16,000 --> 00:24:22,000
The film explores themes of holiday, virgin mary,
nativity, christmas, jesus christ.
